"Saved `deadlock_resolution.md` to the workspace.\n\n**Cause:** Both threads update the same two accounts in opposite order inside deferred transactions. SQLite locks the whole file and a read-first transaction upgrades SHARED → RESERVED on first write, so each thread ends up waiting for a lock the other holds. SQLite breaks the cycle with `SQLITE_BUSY` (`database is locked`).\n\n**Retry strategy:** Roll back the failed transaction, then re-run it up to 3 more times with an escalating short delay (~50 ms × attempt + jitter). Success only counts when both threads commit.\n\nThe doc includes a sequence diagram of the lock cycle and observed results (loser commits by attempt 3, balances stay consistent at 100/100)."